<title>SRI LANKA: Asia Capital up on take-over news.</title>
<headline>Asia Capital up on take-over news.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asia Capital Ltd rose 29 percent, or 2.25 rupees, to 10 rupees as the stock exchange lifted a trading suspension imposed after the firm said it was making an offer to buy Vanik Incorporation Ltd, brokers said.</p>
<p>The price rose on turnover of 5,000 shares.</p>
<p>&quot;The price rise is directly linked to the take-over offer, but it will fall soon on profit-taking,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Asia Capital Ltd on Tuesday offered to buy all the issued shares of Vanik on the basis of 10 rupees in cash and one new share of Asia Capital.  --Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
